# The Dockerfile ends with `COPY ./ ./` into /srv/shiny-server, so anything left
# here is baked into a published image. Shiny Server does not currently serve
# these over HTTP (verified 2026-07-23: app.R, .Rhistory, .RData, .git/config all
# return 404/403, because the directory is treated as a single app), but that is
# a property of the current layout, not a guarantee -- and a published image is
# copyable regardless of what the web server exposes.
.git
.gitattributes
.github

# ~2 MB of saved workspace and 512 lines of console history. Neither is used at
# runtime; both are just the developer's session state.
.RData
.Rhistory

# Stale: pins R 4.3.3 / Bioconductor 3.17 / DESeq2 1.40.2, while this image is
# R 4.5.3 / Bioc 3.22 / DESeq2 1.50.2. Kept in the repo for history but must not
# influence the build. See HANDOVER.md.
renv.lock
renv

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
